  era: "Section 22 \xB7 Social and Religious Reform Movements \xB7 19th \u2013 early 20th century"
  title: Education reforms
  text: Reformers founded schools and colleges for all. Ishwar Chandra Vidyasagar championed girls' schooling and widow remarriage, legalised in 1856; the Phules opened schools for girls and lower castes; and D. K. Karve founded a university for women in 1916.
